{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771196989109,"sessionID":"ses_39c6f4287ffey46zawOx3i1Iz0","part":{"id":"prt_c639109ae001ErRVptwH64ysI4","sessionID":"ses_39c6f4287ffey46zawOx3i1Iz0","messageID":"msg_c6390cf6f001m2ESl5fUaqaPF4","type":"tool","callID":"call_3149a4f86cc94675bbcc9d66","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Explore expert settings spec","prompt":"Study /home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/expert-settings.md thoroughly. What are all the requirements for expert settings? List all parameter categories, their ranges, validation rules, UI requirements, and persistence mechanisms.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_39c6ef63cffe5INlrWzj67XtWn (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nBased on my thorough analysis of `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/expert-settings.md`, here are all the requirements for expert settings:\n\n## Parameter Categories and Ranges\n\n### 1. Movement Detection Parameters\n| Parameter | Default | Range | Description |\n|-----------|---------|-------|-------------|\n| `centroidHistoryLength` | 5 | 3-10 | Generations to track |\n| `movementThreshold` | 0.5 | 0.1-2.0 | Cells to be \"moving\" |\n| `minClusterSize` | 1 | 1-5 | Minimum cells to track |\n\n### 2. Scoring Parameters\n| Parameter | Default | Range | Description |\n|-----------|---------|-------|-------------|\n| `moverPointsPerGeneration` | 10 | 1-100 | Points for movers per generation |\n| `oscillatorPointsPerGeneration` | 2 | 0-20 | Points for oscillators per generation |\n| `scoreMultiplier` | 1.0 | 0.1-5.0 | Global score multiplier |\n\n### 3. Level Generation Parameters\n| Parameter | Default | Range | Description |\n|-----------|---------|-------|-------------|\n| `baseTimeSeconds` | 45 | 10-120 | Base time limit per level |\n| `timeIncrementPerLevel` | 15 | 0-60 | Time added per level |\n| `baseFlux` | 20 | 5-50 | Base flux value |\n| `difficultyScalingMode` | - | enum | 'TIME_ONLY' \\| 'RESOURCE_ONLY' \\| 'MIXED' \\| 'EXTREME' |\n\n### 4. Grid Sizing Parameters\n| Parameter | Default | Range | Description |\n|-----------|---------|-------|-------------|\n| `mobileCellSize` | 18 | 14-24 | Cell size for mobile devices |\n| `desktopCellSize` | 20 | 16-28 | Cell size for desktop devices |\n| `minVisibleCells` | 10 | minimum | Minimum cells visible |\n\n---\n\n## Validation Rules\n\n### Input Validation\n- **Negative numbers**: Must be prevented\n- **Out-of-range values**: Must be blocked/rejected\n- **JSON Schema Validation**: Required for imported settings (using Zod or similar)\n- **Type validation**: All parameters must match their defined types\n\n### Special Validation Cases\n1. **Extreme values**: Require confirmation before applying\n2. **Game-breaking settings**: Show warning if settings would make the game impossible\n3. **Invalid localStorage**: If corrupted JSON is found, fall back to defaults\n\n### Timing Validation\n- Scoring changes: Apply immediately\n- Level generation changes: Apply on next level\n- Grid sizing changes: Apply immediately\n\n---\n\n## UI Requirements\n\n### Access Methods\n| Method | Implementation |\n|--------|----------------|\n| **Keyboard shortcut** | `` ` `` (backtick) for quick access |\n| **Menu path** | \"Settings → Advanced → Expert Mode\" (if menu exists) |\n| **Gesture** | Mobile: triple-tap top-left corner |\n\n### Panel Layout\n- **Position**: Modal overlay (centered or right sidebar)\n- **Organization**: Collapsible groups by category:\n  - Movement Detection\n  - Scoring\n  - Level Generation\n  - Grid Sizing\n\n### Control Types\n- **Sliders**: For numeric range inputs\n- **Number inputs**: For precise value entry\n- **Dropdowns**: For mode selection (e.g., difficulty scaling mode)\n\n### Real-Time Updates\n- Changes apply immediately (no restart required)\n- Visual indicator when value differs from default\n- \"Revert\" button per section\n- Live preview of parameter effects when possible\n\n### Tooltips and Documentation\n- Each parameter must have a tooltip explaining its effect\n\n---\n\n## Persistence Mechanisms\n\n### Storage\n- **Storage location**: `localStorage`\n- **Storage key**: `gol-expert-settings`\n- **Load timing**: On app startup\n\n### Reset Functionality\n- **Reset to defaults** button with confirmation\n- Should warn if game is in progress before resetting\n\n### Export/Import\n- **Export JSON**: Button downloads current configuration as JSON\n- **Import JSON**: File picker to load configuration\n- **Import validation**: Must validate imported JSON against schema before applying\n\n### State Management\n- Recommended: React Context or Zustand for settings state\n- All settings must persist across sessions\n\n---\n\n## Edge Cases Handling\n\n1. **Invalid values**: Prevented by input validation\n2. **Settings while running**: Scoring changes apply immediately; level changes apply on next level\n3. **Reset during game**: Warning required if game is in progress\n4. **Corrupted storage**: Fallback to defaults if localStorage has invalid JSON\n5. **Mobile access**: Gesture detection must not conflict with game controls\n\n---\n\n## Additional Features (Implementation Notes)\n\n- **Presets**: Consider adding presets dropdown (\"Easy\", \"Normal\", \"Hard\", \"Chaos\")\n- **Accessibility**: Expert settings should be accessible but not intrusive\n- **Default behavior**: Default values must create a balanced, playable game\n- **Schema validation**: Use Zod or similar library for robust validation\n</task_result>","title":"Explore expert settings spec","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39c6ef63cffe5INlrWzj67XtWn","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771196975552,"end":1771196989106}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771196996729,"sessionID":"ses_39c6f4287ffey46zawOx3i1Iz0","part":{"id":"prt_c6391097b001PtRu10sRoJEh2v","sessionID":"ses_39c6f4287ffey46zawOx3i1Iz0","messageID":"msg_c6390cf6f001m2ESl5fUaqaPF4","type":"tool","callID":"call_2420e5c6ec594e73a8813213","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Explore audio-sonification spec","prompt":"Study /home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/audio-sonification.md thoroughly. What are all the requirements for audio sonification in this project? List all sound types, their triggers, parameters, and implementation details.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_39c6ef67cffe3cM7Pq52YSvhRA (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nBased on my thorough analysis of the `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/audio-sonification.md` specification, here are all the requirements for the audio sonification system:\n\n---\n\n## **Overview**\nThe audio sonification system generates real-time sounds using the Web Audio API based on simulation birth events and user interactions, providing audio feedback for cellular automaton behavior.\n\n---\n\n## **Sound Engine Interface**\n\n```typescript\ninterface SoundEngine {\n  setEnabled(enabled: boolean): void;\n  setVolume(volume: number): void;\n  setWaveform(waveform: OscillatorType): void;\n  playGenerationSound(bornCount: number, avgRow: number, totalRows: number): void;\n  playInteractionSound(type: 'draw' | 'erase'): void;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## **Sound Types, Triggers, and Parameters**\n\n### **1. Generation Sounds**\n\n| Attribute | Details |\n|-----------|---------|\n| **Trigger** | After each simulation step when `bornCount > 0` |\n| **Purpose** | Provides audio feedback on cellular automaton evolution |\n\n**Pitch Mapping:**\n- **Basis**: Average row position of new births\n- **Formula**: `pitch = (1 - avgRow / totalRows) * frequencyRange`\n- **Higher rows (top)** → Higher pitch\n- **Lower rows (bottom)** → Lower pitch\n\n**Intensity Mapping:**\n- **Basis**: Number of births (`bornCount`)\n- **Behavior**: More births = louder/more prominent sound\n\n**Parameters:**\n```typescript\ninterface GenerationSoundParams {\n  frequency: number;    // Derived from row position\n  duration: number;     // Short, ~100-200ms\n  volume: number;       // baseVolume * bornCount scaling\n  waveform: OscillatorType;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### **2. Draw Sound**\n\n| Attribute | Details |\n|-----------|---------|\n| **Trigger** | When placing a cell (user interaction) |\n| **Pitch** | Higher pitch (~880Hz) |\n| **Duration** | Very short (~50ms) |\n| **Purpose** | Audio feedback for cell creation |\n\n**Parameters:**\n```typescript\ninterface InteractionSoundParams {\n  drawFrequency: number;    // Higher pitch (~880Hz)\n  duration: number;         // Very short (~50ms)\n  volume: number;          // baseVolume\n  waveform: OscillatorType;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### **3. Erase Sound**\n\n| Attribute | Details |\n|-----------|---------|\n| **Trigger** | When removing a cell (user interaction) |\n| **Pitch** | Lower pitch (~440Hz) |\n| **Duration** | Very short (~50ms) |\n| **Purpose** | Audio feedback for cell deletion |\n\n**Parameters:**\n```typescript\ninterface InteractionSoundParams {\n  eraseFrequency: number;   // Lower pitch (~440Hz)\n  duration: number;         // Very short (~50ms)\n  volume: number;          // baseVolume\n  waveform: OscillatorType;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## **Global Audio Parameters**\n\n### **Volume Control**\n- **Range**: 0.0 to 0.5\n- **Default**: 0.1 (10%)\n- **UI Slider**: 10ms steps, displays percentage (volume * 200%)\n\n### **Waveform Types**\n| Waveform | Characteristics | Default |\n|----------|-----------------|---------|\n| `sine` | Smooth, pure tone | Yes |\n| `triangle` | Slightly richer harmonics | No |\n| `square` | Harsh, buzzy tone | No |\n| `sawtooth` | Bright, brassy tone | No |\n\n---\n\n## **Implementation Architecture**\n\n### **SoundEngine Class Structure**\n```typescript\nclass SoundEngine {\n  private audioContext: AudioContext | null = null;\n  private enabled: boolean = true;\n  private volume: number = 0.1;\n  private waveform: OscillatorType = 'sine';\n  \n  // Methods: setEnabled, setVolume, setWaveform, \n  // playGenerationSound, playInteractionSound\n}\n```\n\n### **Sound Generation Process**\n1. **Initialize Context**: Create on first user interaction (browser requirement)\n2. **Create Oscillator**: Generate sound with configured waveform\n3. **Create Gain Node**: Control volume and envelope\n4. **Connect Nodes**: Oscillator → Gain → Destination\n5. **Set Parameters**: Frequency based on data, volume from setting\n6. **Envelope**: Quick attack, exponential decay\n7. **Cleanup**: Stop and disconnect after sound completes\n\n### **Lazy Initialization**\n- AudioContext created on first sound play\n- Handles browser autoplay policies\n- Resumes context if suspended\n\n---\n\n## **Edge Cases**\n\n| Scenario | Handling |\n|----------|----------|\n| No births (`bornCount = 0`) | Sound not triggered |\n| Suspended AudioContext | Resume on next interaction |\n| Volume = 0 | Sounds generated but at 0 gain |\n| Disabled (`enabled = false`) | Engine returns early without generating sounds |\n| Multiple events | Concurrent sounds allowed (polyphonic) |\n\n---\n\n## **Browser Compatibility**\n\n| Platform | Notes |\n|----------|-------|\n| Modern browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge) | Full support |\n| iOS | Requires user gesture to start |\n| Autoplay policy | Context starts suspended |\n\n---\n\n## **Dependencies**\n\n- **Core simulation engine**: Provides birth statistics (`bornCount`, `avgRow`, `totalRows`)\n- **User interaction system**: Triggers draw/erase sounds\n- **UI/overlay system**: Manages volume, waveform, and enabled settings\n\n---\n\n## **Summary Table**\n\n| Sound Type | Trigger | Frequency | Duration | Volume Scaling |\n|------------|---------|-----------|----------|----------------|\n| Generation | Simulation step, bornCount > 0 | Row-mapped, higher rows = higher pitch | 100-200ms | baseVolume * bornCount |\n| Draw | Place cell | ~880Hz (higher) | ~50ms | baseVolume |\n| Erase | Remove cell | ~440Hz (lower) | ~50ms | baseVolume |\n</task_result>","title":"Explore audio-sonification spec","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39c6ef67cffe3cM7Pq52YSvhRA","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771196975488,"end":1771196996727}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771197040489,"sessionID":"ses_39c6f4287ffey46zawOx3i1Iz0","part":{"id":"prt_c63910985001n05qMf9INaXT1H","sessionID":"ses_39c6f4287ffey46zawOx3i1Iz0","messageID":"msg_c6390cf6f001m2ESl5fUaqaPF4","type":"tool","callID":"call_aa28cec606154e7bb4402fac","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Explore visual polish requirements","prompt":"Search the codebase for any specifications related to visual polish, animations, or UI enhancements. Check all specs files and IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md. List all pending visual polish items that need to be implemented.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_39c6ef66affeI2ddDXivWO2cmL (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nBased on my comprehensive search of the codebase, I've identified all pending visual polish, animations, and UI enhancement items. Here's the complete list:\n\n## Pending Visual Polish Items\n\n### 1. **Cell Placement/Removal Animations** (Grid Interaction)\n**Location**: `specs/grid-interaction.md`, `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` (Section 1.9, 4.2)\n- **Cell fade-in animation (0.1s)** when placing a new cell\n- **Cell shrink animation (0.15s)** when removing a cell  \n- **Red flash** on cursor location for invalid actions (e.g., insufficient Flux)\n\n**Status**: Cell preview ghost outline exists (border only), but animations are NOT implemented\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Enhanced Cell Preview Ghost Outline** (Grid Interaction)\n**Location**: `specs/grid-interaction.md` (line 38-40), `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` (Section 4.2)\n- Make the ghost outline **semi-transparent** (currently only a solid border)\n- Ensure it **follows cursor smoothly**\n- Show **different colors** for draw vs erase mode:\n  - Draw mode: `#00ffff` (cyan) - currently implemented\n  - Erase mode: `#ff00ff` (magenta) - currently implemented\n\n**Status**: Basic border outline exists in GridInteraction.tsx (lines 164-178), but lacks semi-transparency and smooth following\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Flux Counter Animations**\n**Location**: `specs/flux-management.md` (line 43, 52), `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` (Section 4.2)\n- **Smooth transitions** when Flux values change\n- **Color coding transitions** with smooth interpolation:\n  - Green/Yellow when plenty remaining (>30%)\n  - Orange when <30% remaining  \n  - Red when 0 remaining\n\n**Status**: Color classes exist in GlassHUD.css (lines 170-180), but smooth transitions are NOT implemented\n\n---\n\n### 4. **UI Toggle Button Integration**\n**Location**: `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` (Section 2.2, line 324)\n- Component exists (`src/components/UIToggleButton.tsx`) but is **not yet integrated** into the game\n\n**Status**: Component exists but not connected to Game component\n\n---\n\n### 5. **Mobile Touch Enhancements**\n**Location**: `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` (Section 4.3, lines 876-891)\n\n#### 5a. Touch-Action Handling\n- Ensure `touch-action: none` on canvas element\n- PreventDefault on all touch events\n- Stop scroll and zoom during interaction\n\n**Status**: Partially implemented - `touchAction: 'none'` exists in CanvasGrid.tsx (line 120), but full PreventDefault implementation incomplete\n\n#### 5b. Minimum Touch Targets\n- Ensure all buttons are ≥44×44px\n- Spacious clickable areas\n\n**Status**: Partially implemented - GlassHUD.css has min-width constraints, but comprehensive audit needed\n\n#### 5c. Touch Ripple Effect (Optional)\n- Visual feedback on touch\n- Radial ripple animation\n\n**Status**: NOT implemented\n\n#### 5d. Mobile Expert Settings Access\n- Triple-tap top-left corner gesture to access expert settings\n- Confirm gesture doesn't conflict with game controls\n\n**Status**: NOT implemented\n\n---\n\n### 6. **Button Hover Effects Polish**\n**Location**: `specs/ui-overlay.md` (line 137)\n\n- Button hover: Scale/brightness transition\n- Current implementation exists in GlassHUD.css (lines 47-51), but verify consistency across all buttons\n\n**Status**: Partially implemented\n\n---\n\n## Already Implemented Visual Features (For Reference)\n\n✅ **Intro glitch effect** - CSS animations in IntroOverlay.css  \n✅ **Transition fade animations** - TransitionOverlay.css (fade-in, fade-out, interstitial)  \n✅ **Score animations** - ScoreDisplay.tsx (pulse, milestone flash, smooth count-up with lerp)  \n✅ **Glass effect polish** - GlassHUD.css (backdrop-filter blur)  \n✅ **Victory screen animations** - VictoryScreen.css (fade-in, pulse, scale animations)  \n✅ **Cell age-based glow effects** - CanvasGrid.tsx (shadow blur based on cell age)  \n✅ **Cell preview ghost outline (basic)** - GridInteraction.tsx (border outline with color coding)  \n✅ **Victory score count-up animation** - VictoryScreen.css (scoreCountUp keyframe)  \n\n---\n\n## Priority Implementation Order\n\n**High Priority:**\n1. Cell placement/removal animations (core feedback)\n2. Flux counter smooth transitions (core UI feedback)\n3. Enhanced cell preview ghost outline (improved UX)\n\n**Medium Priority:**\n4. UI toggle button integration\n5. Touch-action handling completion\n6. Touch ripple effect\n\n**Low Priority:**\n7. Mobile expert settings gesture access\n8. Button hover effects verification across all components\n\n---\n\n## Key Files to Modify\n\n1. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/GridInteraction.tsx` - Add fade-in/shrink animations\n2. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/CanvasGrid.tsx` - Animate cell rendering\n3. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/GlassHUD.tsx` - Integrate UI toggle button\n4. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/styles/GlassHUD.css` - Add smooth Flux color transitions\n5. `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/UIToggleButton.tsx` - Connect to Game component\n</task_result>","title":"Explore visual polish requirements","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39c6ef66affeI2ddDXivWO2cmL","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771196975506,"end":1771197040488}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771197049516,"sessionID":"ses_39c6f4287ffey46zawOx3i1Iz0","part":{"id":"prt_c6391099b001ljzXVDPTs06Gic","sessionID":"ses_39c6f4287ffey46zawOx3i1Iz0","messageID":"msg_c6390cf6f001m2ESl5fUaqaPF4","type":"tool","callID":"call_b4a1a1f3800f4027a4bb2e11","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Explore mobile enhancements","prompt":"Study all specs files and IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md for mobile enhancement requirements. List all mobile-specific features that need to be implemented, including touch handling, responsive design, and mobile-only UI elements.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_39c6ef657ffeqw95wN93ys3fDk (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nBased on my analysis of all spec files and the IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md, here is a comprehensive list of all mobile-specific features that need to be implemented:\n\n---\n\n## **Mobile-Specific Features Implementation List**\n\n### **1. Touch Handling**\n\n#### **Canvas Touch Events (IMPLEMENTED - User Interaction System)**\n- **Touch Start**: Prevent default (stop scrolling), capture first touch position, convert to grid coordinates, trigger interaction handler\n- **Touch Move**: Prevent default (stop scrolling), capture first touch position, convert to grid coordinates, trigger interaction handler\n- **Touch End / Cancel**: Set `isMouseDown` state to false\n- **Multi-touch Support**: Only use first touch (ignore additional touches)\n- **Touch Action Property**: Set `touch-action: none` on canvas element to prevent browser scroll/zoom gestures\n- **Touch Coordinate Mapping**: Screen to grid conversion with canvas scaling and DPR support\n\n#### **Touch Behavior Constraints (PENDING - Grid Interaction)**\n- **Pinch-to-zoom disabled** on game grid\n- **Touch-and-hold to drag not needed** (single click only)\n- **Prevent accidental browser zoom on double-tap**\n- **Touch coordinate validation**: Clamp coordinates to valid range, prevent out-of-bounds access\n\n#### **Touch Visual Feedback (PENDING - Visual Polish)**\n- **Visual ripple effect on touch** (optional)\n- **Cell placement fade-in animation** (0.1s duration)\n- **Cell removal shrink animation** (0.15s duration)\n- **Invalid action red flash** on cursor location\n\n---\n\n### **2. Responsive Design**\n\n#### **Cell Size Adaptation (IMPLEMENTED - Canvas Rendering)**\n- **Mobile devices** (screen width < 768px): 18px cells\n- **Desktop devices** (screen width >= 768px): 20px cells\n- **Cell size updates on window resize**\n- **Grid dimensions recalculate based on cell size**\n- **Ensure minimum 10 cells visible in smallest dimension**\n\n#### **Canvas Scaling (IMPLEMENTED - Canvas Rendering)**\n- **DPR scaling** for sharp rendering using `window.devicePixelRatio`\n- **Window resize handling with coordinate recalculation**\n- **Responsive canvas sizing** adapting to window size\n- **Grid scales accordingly** on resize\n\n#### **UI Responsiveness (PARTIALLY IMPLEMENTED - UI Overlay)**\n- **Desktop**: Full width HUD centered at bottom\n- **Mobile**: Controls may stack or scroll\n- **Responsive glass HUD container** with proper mobile layout\n- **Intro overlay responsive design** for mobile and desktop\n- **Settings panel responsive design** for mobile and desktop\n\n#### **Font and Text Scaling (PENDING - Visual Polish)**\n- **Responsive typography** for mobile and desktop\n- **Proper text scaling** at different zoom levels\n\n---\n\n### **3. Mobile-Only UI Elements**\n\n#### **Mobile Expert Settings Access (PENDING - Expert Settings)**\n- **Triple-tap top-left corner gesture** to access expert settings on mobile\n- **Confirm gesture doesn't conflict with game controls**\n- **Gesture detection logic** separate from keyboard shortcut access\n\n#### **Touch Target Sizing (PARTIALLY IMPLEMENTED - UI Overlay)**\n- **All buttons minimum 44×44px** for mobile accessibility\n- **Spacious clickable areas** for touch interaction\n- **Proper padding and spacing** on mobile controls\n\n#### **Skip Control Adaptation (IMPLEMENTED - Auto-Advance Transitions)**\n- **Skip indicator prompt**: \"Press Space or ESC to skip\" (desktop)\n- **Mobile equivalent**: Need touch-based skip control (tap anywhere to skip)\n\n---\n\n### **4. Mobile Performance Optimizations**\n\n#### **Touch Performance (IMPLEMENTED - User Interaction)**\n- **Event delegation** for efficient touch handling\n- **Prevent default on all touch events** to avoid unnecessary browser processing\n- **Touch coordinate caching** for performance\n- **Minimize re-renders** during touch interactions\n\n#### **Canvas Performance (IMPLEMENTED - Canvas Rendering)**\n- **Optimized rendering pipeline** minimizing context state changes\n- **useCallback dependency tracking** for render optimization\n- **DPR scaling** for sharp mobile rendering\n- **Transform reset** on resize\n\n#### **Movement Detection Performance (IMPLEMENTED)**\n- **Only recompute for changed regions**\n- **Target < 16ms for 60fps** with mobile grid sizes\n- **Circular buffer for history** (efficient memory)\n\n---\n\n### **5. Mobile Accessibility**\n\n#### **Touch Target Requirements (PARTIALLY IMPLEMENTED - UI Overlay)**\n- **Minimum 44×44px touch targets** for all interactive elements\n- **Spacious clickable areas** with adequate spacing\n- **Visible touch feedback** on all interactive elements\n\n#### **Reduced Motion Support (PENDING - Accessibility)**\n- **Respect prefers-reduced-motion media query**\n- **Disable animations when requested**\n- **Simplified visual feedback** for reduced motion\n- **Fade transitions work with reduced motion preferences**\n\n#### **High Contrast Mode (PENDING - Accessibility)**\n- **Toggle for high contrast colors**\n- **Larger text option** for mobile readability\n- **Improved readability** on mobile screens\n\n---\n\n### **6. Mobile-Specific Edge Cases**\n\n#### **Browser Zoom Handling (PARTIALLY IMPLEMENTED)**\n- **Prevent browser zoom on canvas interaction**\n- **Test with all browser zoom levels** to ensure overlay covers fully\n- **Ensure grid maintains aspect ratio** on zoom\n- **Canvas coordinate recalculation** on zoom events\n\n#### **Orientation Changes (PENDING)**\n- **Handle device orientation changes**\n- **Recalculate grid dimensions** on orientation change\n- **Preserve grid state** during orientation change\n- **Proper layout adjustment** for portrait vs landscape\n\n#### **Browser Tab Handling (IMPLEMENTED - Phase Management)**\n- **Timer continues running** when tab inactive during gameplay\n- **Pause timer during transitions** to prevent level advancing unseen\n- **Resume when tab becomes active**\n\n---\n\n### **7. Mobile Input Validation**\n\n#### **Touch Input Constraints (IMPLEMENTED - User Interaction)**\n- **Boundary coordinate validation**: `Math.floor()` ensures valid indices\n- **Canvas resize handling**: Grid dimensions update, coordinates recalculate\n- **Mouse leave canvas**: Set isMouseDown to false to stop drag (analogous for touch)\n\n#### **Flux Validation on Mobile (IMPLEMENTED - Flux Management)**\n- **Deduct 1 Flux per cell placement**\n- **Validate Flux >= 1 before placement**\n- **Visual feedback for insufficient Flux** (red flash)\n- **Queue placements if player touches mid-simulation step**\n\n---\n\n## **Summary Statistics**\n\n- **Total Mobile Features Identified**: 7 categories, 40+ individual features\n- **Fully Implemented**: ~15 features (touch events, responsive cell sizing, DPR scaling, some UI responsiveness)\n- **Partially Implemented**: ~10 features (touch targets, some UI responsiveness, skip controls)\n- **Not Yet Implemented**: ~15+ features (touch ripple, mobile skip gestures, triple-tap expert access, reduced motion, high contrast, orientation handling)\n\n## **Implementation Priority Recommendations**\n\n### **High Priority** (for core mobile experience)\n1. Touch ripple effect feedback\n2. Mobile skip control (tap anywhere to skip transitions)\n3. Triple-tap expert settings access\n4. Complete touch target sizing compliance\n5. Orientation change handling\n\n### **Medium Priority** (for better UX)\n1. Reduced motion support\n2. High contrast mode\n3. Touch-specific animations (fade-in, shrink)\n4. Mobile-specific UI stacking/scrolling\n\n### **Low Priority** (nice-to-have)\n1. Touch gesture documentation\n2. Advanced mobile performance profiling\n3. Mobile-specific accessibility features\n</task_result>","title":"Explore mobile enhancements","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39c6ef657ffeqw95wN93ys3fDk","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771196975525,"end":1771197049515}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771197064050,"sessionID":"ses_39c6f4287ffey46zawOx3i1Iz0","part":{"id":"prt_c639109ec001gfvohyPyAZfaRm","sessionID":"ses_39c6f4287ffey46zawOx3i1Iz0","messageID":"msg_c6390cf6f001m2ESl5fUaqaPF4","type":"tool","callID":"call_584c9869459a473ab3862405","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Check current visual state","prompt":"Analyze all component files in src/components/ to understand current visual implementation. What animations are currently implemented? What visual polish features are missing? Check CSS files too.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_39c6ef600ffeCouFlQzaCqQGSr (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\n## Analysis Complete: Current Visual Implementation\n\nBased on my analysis of all component files and CSS files in `src/components/`, here's a comprehensive breakdown:\n\n---\n\n## **Currently Implemented Animations**\n\n### 1. **TransitionOverlay** (TransitionOverlay.css)\n- `fadeOut` - 2s opacity fade (0 → 1)\n- `fadeIn` - 2s opacity fade (1 → 0)\n- `fadeInScale` - Scale + opacity for interstitial content\n- `fadeOutText` - Fade out with translate up\n- `fadeInText` - Fade in with translate from bottom\n\n### 2. **VictoryScreen** (VictoryScreen.css)\n- `fadeInScaleIn` - Entry animation (scale 0.8→1, fade in)\n- `fadeOutScaleDown` - Exit animation (scale 1→0.9, fade out)\n- `pulse` - Continuous text shadow glow (2s infinite)\n- `scoreCountUp` - Score entry animation with translate\n\n### 3. **ScoreDisplay** (ScoreDisplay.css + JavaScript)\n- `pulse` - Score update animation (scale 1→1.1→1, 0.2s)\n- `milestoneFlash` - Multi-color flash (cyan → yellow → magenta, 0.5s)\n- **JavaScript score counting animation** - Eased number interpolation (200ms)\n\n### 4. **IntroOverlay** (IntroOverlay.css)\n- `glitch` - Random position jitter (0.3s infinite)\n- `glitchSkew` - Skew transformation (0.5s infinite)\n- `fadeInScaleOut` - Exit animation (fade + scale 1→1.1, 1.2s)\n- **CSS pseudo-element glitch effects** - Clip-path animations with color layers (magenta/cyan)\n\n### 5. **SettingsPanel** (SettingsPanel.css)\n- `fadeIn` - Overlay fade (0.2s)\n- `slideUp` - Panel slide up 20px + fade (0.3s)\n\n### 6. **CanvasGrid** (canvasUtils.ts + CanvasGrid.tsx)\n- **Dynamic cell rendering** - Shadow blur varies by age\n- **Color-based age system** - New cells (cyan), young (blue), mature (magenta)\n- **CSS variable for intensity** - `--life-intensity` based on active cell count\n\n### 7. **UI Elements** (GlassHUD.css, VictoryScreen.css, IntroOverlay.css)\n- Button hover transitions (scale, background, border, shadow)\n- Slider thumb hover animations\n- Close button hover effects\n- Shimmer effect on primary buttons (pseudo-element gradient)\n\n---\n\n## **Missing Visual Polish Features**\n\n### **Cell/Grid Animations**\n1. **Cell birth/death animations** - No smooth transition when cells appear or disappear\n2. **Cell hover effects** - Static hover box overlay, no glow or scale\n3. **Cell trail/particle effects** - No particle system for births/deaths\n4. **Glow/bloom enhancement** - Only basic shadow blur, no dynamic bloom\n5. **Grid line animation** - Static grid lines, no pulse or fade effects\n6. **Neighbor highlight** - No indication of cells that will die/born in next generation\n\n### **UI/HUD Polish**\n1. **Countdown timer animation** - No visual timer, only number display\n2. **Flux bar animation** - Text-based flux indicator, no animated bar/gauge\n3. **Progress indicator** - No level progress visualization\n4. **Button press effects** - Basic scale only, no ripple or particle burst\n5. **Achievement toasts** - No notification animations for milestones\n6. **Phase change transitions** - No transition between PLANNING → COUNTDOWN → RUNNING\n7. **Victory confetti** - No celebration particles\n\n### **Score/Feedback Polish**\n1. **Floating score text** - No floating \"+10\" or \"+50\" animations on score gain\n2. **Combo/streak indicators** - No visual combo counter\n3. **Pattern detection UI** - Mover/oscillator status not displayed in UI (computed but not shown)\n4. **Level complete fanfare** - Only fade overlay, no dramatic effect\n5. **Score breakdown animation** - Breakdown exists but is static, no entry animations\n\n### **Background/Atmosphere**\n1. **Dynamic background** - Static dark background\n2. **Ambient particles** - No background particle effects\n3. **Vignette/focus effects** - No focus management\n4. **Color temperature** - No mood color changes based on phase/score\n5. **Screen shake** - No shake on births/deaths\n\n### **Micro-interactions**\n1. **Hover delays** - All hover effects are instant\n2. **Disabled state feedback** - Buttons just fade out, no distinct disabled style\n3. **Loading states** - No loading/skeleton animations\n4. **Empty state guidance** - No hint when grid is empty\n\n### **Typography**\n1. **Kinetic typography** - Only basic scale/translate on some text\n2. **Character-by-character reveals** - No text reveal animations\n3. **Number rollup** - Only score has number animation, not timer/generation\n\n### **Accessibility Polish**\n1. **Reduced motion** - No `prefers-reduced-motion` media query\n2. **Focus indicators** - Custom focus styles not visible\n3. **High contrast mode** - No high contrast theme support\n\n---\n\n## **Summary**\n\n**Strengths:**\n- Good overlay transitions (intro, victory, settings)\n- Polished victory screen with pulsing glow\n- Nice glitch effect on intro\n- Score counting animation is smooth\n- Glass morphism UI elements are well-styled\n\n**Areas for Enhancement:**\n- **Grid visualization needs the most work** - cells appear/disappear instantly with no animation\n- **Missing feedback animations** - births/deaths, score gains, phase changes\n- **HUD could be more dynamic** - animated bars, countdown visual\n- **Background is completely static** - no ambient effects\n- **Micro-interactions are minimal** - no particles, ripples, or tactile feedback\n\nThe codebase has a solid foundation with glassmorphism UI and core overlay animations, but the grid itself (the main game element) lacks visual polish, which would significantly improve the overall experience.\n</task_result>","title":"Check current visual state","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39c6ef600ffeCouFlQzaCqQGSr","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771196975612,"end":1771197064048}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771197068793,"sessionID":"ses_39c6f4287ffey46zawOx3i1Iz0","part":{"id":"prt_c639109cc001gj6gdfPWwKDQ8w","sessionID":"ses_39c6f4287ffey46zawOx3i1Iz0","messageID":"msg_c6390cf6f001m2ESl5fUaqaPF4","type":"tool","callID":"call_ffe4d114b0f24a24bdb6159f","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Check current audio implementation","prompt":"Analyze src/lib/audio.ts and src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx to understand the current audio implementation. What sounds are currently implemented? What sounds are missing based on the specs? What hooks are available for connecting the missing sounds?","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_39c6ef619ffefzSRiWmYfV5ZZV (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nBased on my analysis of the audio implementation files, here's a comprehensive breakdown:\n\n---\n\n## Current Audio Implementation (src/lib/audio.ts)\n\n### Sounds Currently Implemented:\n\n1. **`playGenerationSound`** (Lines 42-70)\n   - Trigger: After each simulation step with bornCount > 0\n   - Frequency: Mapped to average row position (top = higher pitch, bottom = lower pitch)\n   - Intensity: Based on bornCount (volume = baseVolume * sqrt(bornCount))\n   - Duration: 150ms\n\n2. **`playInteractionSound`** (Lines 72-99)\n   - Trigger: When user draws/erases cells\n   - Draw sound: 880Hz (higher pitch)\n   - Erase sound: 440Hz (lower pitch)\n   - Duration: 50ms\n\n3. **`playLevelCompleteSound`** (Lines 101-133)\n   - Trigger: When a level is finished\n   - Dual oscillator at 523.25Hz + 659.25Hz (harmony)\n   - Duration: 300ms\n\n4. **`playLevelStartSound`** (Lines 135-161)\n   - Trigger: When transitioning to a new level\n   - Single oscillator at 440Hz\n   - Duration: 200ms\n\n5. **`playTransitionSound`** (Lines 163-190)\n   - Trigger: During fade transitions\n   - Fade-out: 300Hz\n   - Fade-in: 400Hz\n   - Duration: 150ms\n\n6. **`playSimulationStartSound`** (Lines 192-218)\n   - Trigger: When simulation starts (countdown → RUNNING)\n   - Single oscillator at 330Hz\n   - Duration: 100ms\n\n---\n\n## Missing Sound Based on Specs:\n\n### 1. **Insufficient Flux Error Sound**\n- **Spec Reference**: `specs/flux-management.md` (Lines 46-54)\n- **Description**: \"Audio: Error/denied sound\" when Flux reaches 0 and user tries to place cells\n- **Status**: NOT IMPLEMENTED\n- **Where to Connect**: In `GridInteraction.tsx` when `canPlaceCell(flux)` returns false\n\n---\n\n## Audio Integration Status (from Game.tsx & GridInteraction.tsx)\n\nAll 6 implemented sounds ARE already connected to the application:\n\n| Sound Method | Hook/Integration Point | Status |\n|-------------|----------------------|--------|\n| `playGenerationSound` | Game.tsx: `handleSimulationStep` (line 169) | Connected ✓ |\n| `playInteractionSound` | GridInteraction.tsx: `handleCellClick` (lines 45, 55, 66) | Connected ✓ |\n| `playLevelCompleteSound` | Game.tsx: FINISHED phase (line 142) | Connected ✓ |\n| `playLevelStartSound` | Game.tsx: `handleTransitionComplete` (line 92) | Connected ✓ |\n| `playTransitionSound` | useTransition hook: `onTransitionSound` callback (lines 73-75, 119) | Connected ✓ |\n| `playSimulationStartSound` | Game.tsx: Phase change effect (line 132) | Connected ✓ |\n\n---\n\n## Available Hooks for Connecting Missing Sounds:\n\n### For Insufficient Flux Error Sound:\n\n**Option 1: Add to GridInteraction component**\n- **File**: `src/components/GridInteraction.tsx`\n- **Location**: In the `handleCellClick` callback (around lines 42-63)\n- **When**: After checking `canPlaceCell(flux)` and it returns false\n- **Current code**:\n```typescript\n} else {\n  if (canPlaceCell(flux)) {\n    onInteractionSound?.('draw')\n    // ... placement logic\n  }\n  // MISSING: else branch for insufficient flux\n}\n```\n\n**Option 2: Add new callback prop to GridInteraction**\n- Prop name: `onFluxErrorSound`\n- Type: `() => void`\n- Connect in Game.tsx: `soundEngineRef.current?.playFluxErrorSound()`\n- Need to add method to SoundEngine class\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Plan for Missing Sound:\n\nTo add the insufficient Flux error sound:\n\n1. **Add method to SoundEngine** (src/lib/audio.ts):\n```typescript\nplayFluxErrorSound(): void {\n  if (!this.enabled) return;\n  this.ensureAudioContext();\n  // Create error/denied sound (e.g., low frequency, buzzy tone)\n}\n```\n\n2. **Add callback to GridInteraction props**:\n```typescript\ninterface GridInteractionProps {\n  // ... existing props\n  onFluxErrorSound?: () => void;\n}\n```\n\n3. **Call in GridInteraction when placement blocked**:\n```typescript\nif (!canPlaceCell(flux)) {\n  onFluxErrorSound?.();\n  // Visual feedback already exists\n  return;\n}\n```\n\n4. **Connect in Game component**:\n```typescript\nconst handleFluxErrorSound = useCallback(() => {\n  soundEngineRef.current?.playFluxErrorSound();\n}, []);\n\n<GridInteraction onFluxErrorSound={handleFluxErrorSound} ... />\n```\n\n---\n\n## Summary:\n\n- **Implemented Sounds**: 6/7 (86%)\n- **Missing Sound**: Insufficient Flux error sound\n- **Integration Quality**: Excellent - all implemented sounds are properly connected\n- **Hook Availability**: Clear integration points exist in both GridInteraction and Game components\n- **Implementation Effort**: Low - only need to add one sound method and connect it via existing callback pattern\n</task_result>","title":"Check current audio implementation","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39c6ef619ffefzSRiWmYfV5ZZV","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771196975588,"end":1771197068791}}}}
